## Plan-doc fixes (for you to fold into `ta-anchor-refactor-v2-plan.md`)

**V9 — should-fix BEFORE coding (executability; this is Dean's own verify-item).**
The load-bearing per-variant (b)-fallback rule is stated two contradictory ways:
- §2 (L195–211) gates it on enablement (under `[TA]`-only → PRC=0, not sat's (b)).
- §6 step 3 (L409–412), the section the coder implements from, states it **unconditionally**:
  "…with the per-variant fallback to sat's own (b) when binding lacks that variant."
A literal §6 build always falls back to sat's (b), contradicting §2. Test 2 (L218–220) is a red-test
backstop, but §6 should be self-consistent with §2 up front. Fix: §6 step 3 → "fallback to sat's (b)
**only when saturation is enabled** (per the §2 table); under `[TA]`-only a variant the binding
analyzer omits (with no persisted TA PRC) gets **PRC = 0**, not sat's (b)." The getter already has
`satNR.Enabled` in scope, so the gate is cleanly expressible.

**V8 — should-fix (doc accuracy).**
§7c heading (L729), §7c body (L731–734), and §3 (L262–263) attribute `[sat,TA]` scale-from-zero to
§7b. But in `[sat,TA]` binding = sat, so the anchor's (b) — which drives picker *selectability* —
comes from **sat's own** zero-replica emission (`aggregateByVariant` stored-capacity/compatible-sibling
estimate), not §7b's TA PRC. §7b's `[sat,TA]` role is only feeding the *combine demand* side. §7b is
the proactive *selectability* complement for **`[TA]`-only only**. (Your own V6 note L1129–1131 already
states "in default and `[sat,TA]`, binding = sat, so (b) already comes from sat.") Fix: scope the
"covered via §7b" claim (heading L729; L732–734; §3 L262) to `[TA]`-only for the proactive-selectability
statement, and describe §7b's `[sat,TA]` role precisely. Sub-note: "all-variants fallback" (L262) is
stale pre-`2e83c7fe` wording — §7b emits only for previously-live-now-zero (L736–738); call it
"previously-live PRC-only emission."

**V11 — minor (doc completeness).**
§12 (L999–1001) scopes the sat `Cost=0` blast radius to "`[saturation]`-only always, and now `[TA]`-only
too" — omits `[sat,TA]`. `[sat,TA]` binds sat, so a returning zero-replica variant there also gets
Cost=0 + PRC>0 → same mis-ranking. Add `[sat,TA]` to the L1001 enumeration (all three sat/TA configs).

**V10 — minor (executability).**
Test 7 (L710–716) and Test 10 (L717–723) don't name the concrete test harness/layer. Test 10 =
optimizer-selection layer (pipeline cost picker, `cost_aware_optimizer`); Test 7 = analyzer layer
(`throughput` emission). Name the harness per test for coder orientation (the plan is otherwise exact
about file paths).

